  "summary": "uwu ( ), also stylized UwU, is an emoticon representing a cute face.",
  "description": "uwu ( ), also stylized UwU, is an emoticon representing a cute face. The u characters represent closed eyes, while the w represents a cat mouth. It is used to express various warm, happy, or affectionate feelings.",
  "culturalContext": "The emoticon uwu is known to date back as far as April 11, 2000, when it was used by furry artist Ghislain Deslierres in a post on the furry art site VCL (Vixen Controlled Library). A 2005 anime fanfiction contained another early use of the word. The origin of the term is unknown, with many people believing it to originate in Internet chat rooms. By 2014, the emoticon had spread across the Internet into Tumblr, becoming an Internet subculture.\n\nThe word uwu is included in the Royal Spanish Academy's word observatory, defined as an \"emoticon used to show happiness or tenderness\".",
